invariant: INV-72
file: src/hkdf.c
catches: hash_test
reason: hmac_sha512 hashes a key longer than SHA-512's block with SHA-384,
  where RFC 2104 section 2 hashes it with the HMAC's own hash. Every
  HMAC-SHA-512 and HKDF-SHA-512 under such a key is then wrong, and the
  first 48 bytes of the hashed key still look like a key. Wycheproof's
  suite has no key past 65 bytes, so it passes. RFC 4231's test cases 6
  and 7, whose key is 131 bytes, fail in bin/hash_test.

--- old
    if (key_len > SHA512_BLOCK) {
        sha512_of(key, key_len, k);
--- new
    if (key_len > SHA512_BLOCK) {
        sha384_of(key, key_len, k);
